Why Standalone works, but your scripted flow does not
✅ Standalone (UI) behavior — why it goes to Pending Return
When you create a Vendor Return Authorization manually from the UI, you are actually doing this:

Purchase Order → Return Authorization (Transform)

Even though you don’t see it technically, NetSuite internally does a transaction transform.
That transform does three critical things automatically:

Links the VRA to the exact PO line IDs (orderline)
Confirms the item was received and is return‑eligible
Marks the return as physical inventory movement

Because of this, when you click Authorize Return, NetSuite knows:

Which inventory lot/bin/receipt to reverse
That goods still need to be sent back

✅ Result: Pending Return

❌ Scripted behavior — why it goes to Pending Credit
In your scripted flow, this is what happens:

NCR → Suitelet
Suitelet opens a NEW Vendor Return Authorization
User Event sets:

vendor
item
quantity
PO reference



Even if:

the item is an inventory item
the PO exists
quantities are correct

❌ NetSuite still sees this as a brand‑new transaction, NOT a transformed one.
What is missing internally?

❌ No PO line‑level linkage
❌ No receipt/fulfillment lineage
❌ No inventory reversal context

So NetSuite concludes:

“There is nothing to physically return. This is a financial adjustment only.”

✅ Result: Pending Credit

✅ The key point (this resolves the confusion)

createdfrom = PO is NOT the same as “created FROM the PO”.


Standalone UI → real transform
Script using record.create() → reference only

That’s why:

UI works ✅
Script does not ❌
